 ## Lifetime
 
 Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
@@ -9,8 +12,18 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The web app uses the shared `sessions` instance in `larder/session_store.py`
+([keep sessions in memory](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-memory.md)).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Sessions are isolated to a web process. Use a single process or route each member consistently to the same
+  process to avoid losing their login between requests.
+- A restart or deploy discards sessions; members must sign in again. Sessions previously stored in Postgres are
+  not loaded by the memory store.
+- The store does not remove expired entries automatically. Expiry checks remain the caller's responsibility;
+  restarting the process clears retained entries but also ends active sessions.
 
